From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: arm926ejs: let the SoC clean the whole D-cache

flush_dcache_all() cleans the D-cache with the ARM926 test-and-clean
loop. Compatible cores such as the Faraday FA626TE clean it with a single
clean-and-invalidate-all operation instead, so make the function weak for
the SoC to replace.

diff --git a/arch/arm/cpu/arm926ejs/cache.c b/arch/arm/cpu/arm926ejs/cache.c
index 71b8ad0f..b8a4d6e2 100644
--- a/arch/arm/cpu/arm926ejs/cache.c
+++ b/arch/arm/cpu/arm926ejs/cache.c
@@ -14,7 +14,11 @@ void invalidate_dcache_all(void)
 	asm volatile("mcr p15, 0, %0, c7, c6, 0\n" : : "r"(0));
 }
 
-void flush_dcache_all(void)
+/*
+ * The test-and-clean loop is an ARM926 feature; a compatible core that cleans
+ * its D-cache another way can provide its own.
+ */
+__weak void flush_dcache_all(void)
 {
 	asm volatile(
 		"0:"
